How would you design a disaster recovery strategy for Azure Event Hubs?
To design disaster recovery for Azure Event Hubs, I would use the Geo-Disaster Recovery feature.

This involves creating a primary Event Hubs namespace in one Azure region and a secondary namespace in another region. Geo-DR replicates metadata such as Event Hub configurations, consumer groups, and access policies between the two namespaces.

A DNS alias is used so applications connect through the alias instead of directly to the namespace. During failover, the secondary namespace becomes the new primary and the alias automatically points to it.

One important limitation is that Geo-DR does not replicate actual event data, so producers should implement retry logic to resend any in-flight events that may be lost during failover.

For durable event backup, I would enable Event Hubs Capture to store all events in Azure Blob Storage or Azure Data Lake.

I would also regularly test failover scenarios in non-production environments to verify reconnection, DNS propagation, and recovery procedures.
