How would you implement a solution to monitor and alert on the performance of an Azure Event Hubs instance?
To monitor Azure Event Hubs performance, I would use Azure Monitor, which automatically collects platform metrics and logs.
I would track important metrics such as Incoming Messages, Outgoing Messages, Throttled Requests, Server Errors, and Capture Lag.
For alerting, I would create Azure Monitor alert rules. For example, if throttled requests become greater than zero or incoming traffic suddenly drops below the normal baseline, an alert can be sent through email, Teams, or SMS.
I would also enable Diagnostic Settings to send logs to a Log Analytics workspace. This allows advanced querying and troubleshooting using Kusto Query Language (KQL).
For visualization, I would create Azure Dashboards or Grafana dashboards so the operations team can monitor all Event Hubs namespaces from a single place.
