“How can you secure data in transit when using Azure Event Hubs?”
To secure data in transit with Azure Event Hubs, I would first rely on TLS 1.2 encryption, which is enabled by default for all communication between clients and Event Hubs.
For access control, I would use Azure Active Directory RBAC roles such as Azure Event Hubs Data Sender and Data Receiver because identity-based authentication is more secure than shared keys.
If SAS tokens are used, I would configure them with limited permissions and expiration times to follow the principle of least privilege.
To improve network security, I would use Private Link or Virtual Network integration so traffic stays within Azure private networks instead of the public internet.
In highly secure environments, I would disable public endpoints completely and allow access only through private networking.
