Design Real-Time Pipeline Using Event Hubs and Power BI
A real-time analytics pipeline can be designed using Azure Event Hubs, Azure Stream Analytics, and Power BI.
First, Azure Event Hubs ingests streaming data from applications, IoT devices, or microservices.
Then Azure Stream Analytics processes the stream in real time by applying filtering, transformations, and window-based aggregations such as tumbling or hopping windows.
The processed output is sent to Power BI as a streaming dataset.
Power BI dashboards can then display live metrics such as active users, sales per minute, or sensor readings.
I would configure Event Hub partitions based on expected throughput and enable checkpointing in Stream Analytics to ensure reliable processing and recovery.
