2. How would you handle duplicate events in Azure Event Hubs?
Azure Event Hubs provides at-least-once delivery, so duplicate events are possible.

To handle this, I would design the consumer to be idempotent, meaning processing the same event multiple times should produce the same result.

Each event should contain a unique event ID generated by the producer.

The consumer can maintain a processed-event store using Redis or a database table to track already processed IDs.

If the same event arrives again, the consumer skips processing.

I would also use checkpointing so consumers resume from the last processed offset after failures.

For downstream systems, I would prefer upsert operations instead of plain inserts to avoid duplicate records.
