Describe a scenario where you would use Azure Data Factory with Azure Event Hubs
Azure Data Factory and Azure Event Hubs are commonly used together when we need both batch and real-time processing.

For example, ADF can run scheduled pipelines to load reference data like customer or product information from SQL Server into Azure Storage.

At the same time, Azure Event Hubs can ingest real-time events such as website clicks or IoT sensor data.

Then services like Stream Analytics can combine the streaming events with the batch reference data to generate enriched real-time analytics.

ADF can also trigger downstream pipelines automatically when new files arrive from Event Hub consumers.

